     "transpiration",
     "stomata",
     "photosynthesis"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Plants take in water through roots and give out extra water as vapour through tiny holes in leaves called stomata. This is transpiration. It cools the plant and pulls water upwards.\nPlants make food by photosynthesis, using sunlight, water and carbon dioxide, and release oxygen.\nSome plants like insectivorous pitcher plants trap insects for extra nutrients."
    }
